The implementation in `src/tag_utils.ts` is:
```typescript
export function normalizeTag(tag: string): string {
  return tag
    .trim()
    .toLowerCase()
    .replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-")
    .replace(/^-+|-+$/g, "");
}
```

This correctly:
1. Trims whitespace with `.trim()`
2. Lowercases with `.toLowerCase()`
3. Collapses non-alphanumeric runs into single dashes with `.replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, "-")` (note: after lowercasing, only a-z and 0-9 are alphanumeric)
4. Strips leading/trailing dashes with `.replace(/^-+|-+$/g, "")`

